<div class="c"><h1 class="redstar">Poetry By:Scream</h1></div><h2 class="c">Name</h2><p>Yes i've done all these anonymous poems<br>My friends call me Scream<br>My close friends call me Nate<br>Some of you know me<br>Some of you don't<br>Do I really have any friends?<br>Sometimes i wonder<br>I trust no one but the webmaster<br>He knows a great deal about me<br>Thank you for being a friend <br>You truly do know my true name<br><br></p><hr width="50%" class="redstar"><h2 class="c">Happy</h2><p>Do you expect happiness?<br>Do you wonder why you've never seen it before?<br>Do you wonder why your life has been less than optimal?<br>That's because you'll never see it<br>For you, It will never exist<br>Don't worry others will see it<br>Just not you<br>You know it's true<br>The facts are all in<br>Case Dismissed</p><hr width="50%" class="redstar"><h2 class="c">Sunday Morning</h2><p>Tis a bright and wonderful sunday morning<br>Children laugh and play<br>People shake hands<br>Praising their entity<br>While miles away sits a man<br>Planning his demise for the world<br>On a day of praise no less<br><br>It brings a calmess to him<br>Showing him that he can make his own fate<br>He tries numerous times<br>To make her see<br>She doesnt see<br>She'll never see<br><br>Closed minded<br>Why waste the time?<br>Is it because he loved her?<br>Is it because he was lonely?<br>Who knows?<br><br>She found something <br>Showing her pathetic little heart<br>She thinks she loves again<br>She never loved to start with<br>She'll never love<br>She is incapable of love<br><br>He laughs at this feeling and knows that she will one day cause her own world to crash^M<br>He will sit back and think about all the times he waited on her to come around<br>He laughs again<br>Knowing that it was not worth the time<br>With the red flowing down his arm<br>He once again laughs<br>He knows that he will become one with nature shortly<br>He just wants to see pain<br>He wants to know that she is experiencing pain<br>Like he did before her<br>He can die in peace knowing that her soul is damned<br>Seeing her lover<br>He wishes for him to drive himself crazy<br>Just a glimpse before he passes<br>To know that they will never have happiness is worth more than his own life<br>To know that they will destroy eachother brings a tears of joy to his saturated eye<br>Peace endures him for on this sunday morning an entity let him see <br>Exactly what he had thought<br>Peace endures him as he becomes one with nature once more<br>On this Sunday morning, his faith has been restored<br></p><hr width="50%" class="redstar"><h2 class="c">Madness</h2><p>As a child my mind lay awake<br>Thoughts of happiness filled me<br>As I evolved not only in mind but in spirit<br>Things became clear to me<br><br>To have the opportunity to feel<br>To have the opportunity to love<br>To have the opportunity to be loved<br><br>She came to me in my dreams<br>A dream that some call life<br>More or less a nightmare within itself<br>Showing me what I had forever longed for<br><br>Ripped open from the chest<br>The dawn approaches me this day<br>What seemed like greatness<br>Was a cruel joke<br><br>Having to see my mistake haunting me<br>Cringing with hate<br>Burning with Rage<br>Wanting to end all possibilities<br>For the ones who wished to feel <br>What I had wanted before them<br>Is this evil, to feel this way? <br>I hardly doubt it<br>I see it mainly as a release <br>From humanities downfall <br>All because of this feeling I longed for<br>No one must feel the way I do<br>No one has the mind and patience that I have<br>They say they do<br>They are pathetic<br>No excuse for stupidity in my world<br>And it is MY world<br>You pathetic humans shall see<br>I will do what I must in order to make everyone<br>As miserable as me<br>If it means lying<br>If it means destroying<br>If it means that it will cause the end of existence<br>Yes I will go that far to show them all<br><br>Your new love is trivial<br>It can never be as pure as mine<br>Wanting nothing but a wonderful time<br>Treating all women as possessions<br>Hiding behind the words and the sweetness<br>Confessing Love prematurely to her<br>I can smell it a mile away<br>Will I say anything about it?<br>Not a chance<br>I want to see the essence of pain lurk around their dark hearts<br>Only I am good<br>They are bad<br>They are unclean<br>Therefore deserve to pay for their crimes against me<br><br>As I look around this room<br>The room I built with my own selfishness<br>I wonder what the buckles and the extra long sleeves on this jacket are for<br>I wonder why I even care<br>I think to myself<br>&nbsp;Pathetic fools, why must you deny your doom?&nbsp;<br>All because she needed something that was right in front of her<br><br>Here in this room my selfishness fades<br>I can still help<br>To save others from pain<br>God...To save them from the pain<br>The pain is too much for the average soul<br>I have seen darkness in it's pure form<br>It materialized in the form of Love<br>Only the evil can sense the evil<br><br>No one is safe from this retched feeling<br>The haunting is the worst part<br>Understand what this means<br>Before it's too late<br>You know what you must do <br><br><br></p><hr width="50%" class="redstar"></body>
